Good day,

I encountered a case where a bad font size
is asked for.

When I write

\documentstyle[12pt]{article}
\begin{document}
{\tiny\tt something}
\end{document}

I ask for OT1/cmtt/m/n at 7pt,
according to the definition of tiny in art12.sty.

So, I am referring to the file OT1cmtt.fd
where it is written:

\DeclareFontShape{OT1}{cmtt}{m}{n}
     {
      <5><6><7><8>cmtt8 <9> cmtt9
      <10><10.95>cmtt10
      <12><14.4><17.28><20.74><24.88>cmtt12
      }{}

As I am working in 300dpi, xdvi or dvips
should look for the file cmtt8.262pk (262.5=(7/8)*300).
Unfortunately, it looks for cmtt8.225pk ((3/4)*300).

Is this normal ?

Denis.

